{"message_id": "ai-response-1750663538915", "feedback": "up", "content": "## Overview of Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY)\n### Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY) Overview\nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana, also known as PMAY, is a flagship Government of India housing mission launched in 2015 with the goal of achieving \"Housing for All\" by 2022. It has two components: PMAY\u2013Urban (PMAY\u2013U) and PMAY\u2013Gramin (PMAY\u2013G), providing pucca houses to economically weaker, low-income, and middle-income households in urban and rural areas respectively.\n\n### Key Features\n- **One Home Per Family**: Both schemes emphasize one home per family.\n- **Socio-Economic Surveys and Eligibility Checks**: Beneficiaries are selected through socio-economic surveys and strict eligibility checks.\n- **Objectives**: PMAY\u2013U aims to alleviate urban housing shortages, while PMAY\u2013G provides pucca houses to the poorest rural households.\n\n### Key Components\n- **PMAY Urban (PMAY-U)**: Focuses on addressing acute urban housing shortages among EWS/LIG/MIG groups and promises access to durable houses.\n- **PMAY Gramin (PMAY-G)**: Provides pucca houses to the poorest rural households, emphasizing inclusive urban living and quality housing.\n\n### Tools\n- **PMAY Mobile Application**: A convenient way to interact with PMAY mission, allowing users to search for information on mobile devices or visit the official website.\n- **Features of PMAY Mobile App**:\n  - Upload photos/selfies of homes\n  - Share videos of experiences with PMAY\n  - Access scheme details and updates\n  - Track PMAY progress\n\n### Contacts\n- To download the PMAY mobile application, users can search for \"PMAY Urban\" on their device's app store or visit the official website.\n- For any technical issues, contact the respective helpdesk numbers provided.\n\n### Recent Updates\n- As of January 2025, 118.64 lakh houses have been sanctioned under PMAY-U.\n- The scheme covers 4,618 cities/urban local bodies across India and has provided pucca houses to 112.50 lakh households.\n\n### Coverage\n- PMAY\u2013U serves 4,618 Cities/Urban Local Bodies across India as of January 2025.\n- As of January 2025, a total of 118.64 lakh houses have been sanctioned under PMAY\u2013U.\n- A total of 90.25 lakh houses have been completed and delivered to beneficiaries.\n\n### grievance Redressal\n- For any grievances or complaints related to PMAY schemes, users can contact:\n  - PMAY Helpline: 1800-11-6163 (HUDCO) or 1800-11-3377/3388 (NHB)\n  - Implementing Agency Contact Information\n  - Grievance Redressal Cell of your state's housing department\n\n### Links\n- All major aspects of PMAY scheme, including applications, tracking, grievances, and technical support, are covered on the official portals.\n- Regular updates and notifications are posted.\n\n### Coverage Information\n- PMAY\u2013U covers all urban local bodies (ULBs) across India as of January 2025.\n- As of January 2025, a total of 118.64 lakh houses have been sanctioned under PMAY\u2013U."}
